WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.875


2
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:32.166
<b>Here Krishna says</b>

3
00:00:32.166 --> 00:00:35.583
<b>that a determined intellect </b>
<b>remains focused on one goal,</b>

4
00:00:35.583 --> 00:00:40.166
<b>while an uncertain mind </b>
<b>runs in many directions,</b>

5
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:43.333
<b>remaining consumed by endless thoughts.</b>

6
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:45.666
<b>Krishna wishes to clarify here</b>

7
00:00:45.666 --> 00:00:50.750
<b>that the complete benefit of selfless action </b>
<b>can only be attained by one who is focused,</b>

8
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.916
<b>who is centered solely on the goal.</b>

9
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.166
<b>Understanding intellect and mind here</b>

10
00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:05.708
<b>intellect gives us wisdom and </b>
<b>decision-making power,</b>

11
00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:06.750
<b>while the mind</b>

12
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:13.125
<b>helps us preserve and express our </b>
<b>emotions, desires, and experiences.</b>

13
00:01:13.125 --> 00:01:15.375
<b>The mind is a servant of intellect,</b>

14
00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:18.250
<b>and the body is a servant of the mind.</b>

15
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.625
<b>In this, intellect is supreme,</b>

16
00:01:20.625 --> 00:01:23.000
<b>person follows its thinking alone.</b>

17
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.041
<b>That's why it's said,</b>

18
00:01:25.041 --> 00:01:28.375
<b>'To change life, change your thinking.'</b>

19
00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:32.916
<b>When intellect or thought changes, </b>
<b>everything will change automatically.</b>

20
00:01:32.916 --> 00:01:33.833
<b>But</b>

21
00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:35.583
<b>this is also true that</b>

22
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:39.125
<b>"When the master is unreliable, </b>
<b>the servant becomes careless." </b>

23
00:01:39.125 --> 00:01:42.916
<b>If the master-like intellect </b>
<b>remains unstable, uncertain,</b>

24
00:01:42.916 --> 00:01:48.083
<b>then the mind will not only wander here </b>
<b>and there but will also lead the person astray.</b>

25
00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:51.833
<b>Here Krishna describes two types of people:</b>

26
00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:52.791
<b>First are</b>

27
00:01:52.791 --> 00:01:57.916
<b>those who nourish their intellect,</b>
<b>their wisdom, and improve it.</b>

28
00:01:57.916 --> 00:02:02.125
<b>Here the intellect will be strong, focused,</b>
<b>and when this happens, </b>

29
00:02:02.125 --> 00:02:09.333
<b>a person will move towards their goal like </b>
<b>an arrow, without worrying about the outcome.</b>

30
00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:14.083
<b>This is very important for </b>
<b>the path of selfless action.</b>

31
00:02:14.083 --> 00:02:16.291
<b>The second type of people are </b>

32
00:02:16.291 --> 00:02:19.083
<b>those who don't nourish </b>
<b>their intellect and wisdom.</b>

33
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.916
<b>In this situation, they don't remain focused.</b>

34
00:02:21.916 --> 00:02:24.791
<b>And the mind runs in every direction.</b>

35
00:02:24.791 --> 00:02:31.583
<b>The mind becomes consumed by endless</b>
<b>thoughts of pleasure, pain, profit, and loss.</b>

36
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.541
<b>Humans today live in a present</b>

37
00:02:40.541 --> 00:02:45.375
<b>where their attention is pulled </b>
<b>in countless directions,</b>

38
00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:50.791
<b>with numerous temptations</b>
<b>drawing their senses.</b>

39
00:02:50.791 --> 00:02:55.541
<b>In such times, staying focused</b>
<b>becomes extremely difficult,</b>

40
00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:59.291
<b>and becoming confused becomes very easy.</b>

41
00:02:59.291 --> 00:03:00.541
<b>But</b>

42
00:03:00.541 --> 00:03:04.416
<b>why does one become confused?</b>

43
00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:08.708
<b>Is it because these external</b>
<b>temptations are too powerful?</b>

44
00:03:08.708 --> 00:03:09.916
<b>Or</b>

45
00:03:09.916 --> 00:03:16.416
<b>is the real reason hidden within </b>
<b>the person themselves?</b>

46
00:03:16.416 --> 00:03:18.708
<b>Our mind is powerful,</b>

47
00:03:18.708 --> 00:03:23.750
<b>but it needs a purpose.</b>

48
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.083
<b>If it doesn't find purpose,</b>

49
00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:28.166
<b>it doesn't find direction,</b>

50
00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:31.083
<b>and if it doesn't find direction,</b>

51
00:03:31.083 --> 00:03:35.666
<b>the mind's strength becomes wasted.</b>

52
00:03:35.666 --> 00:03:36.958
<b>However,</b>

53
00:03:36.958 --> 00:03:39.208
<b>if the purpose is right,</b>

54
00:03:39.208 --> 00:03:41.291
<b>the mind's direction will be right,</b>

55
00:03:41.291 --> 00:03:43.375
<b>the mind won't become confused.</b>

56
00:03:43.375 --> 00:03:48.833
<b>In such a state, the mind is capable of anything.</b>

57
00:03:48.833 --> 00:03:50.541
<b>So the truth is</b>

58
00:03:50.541 --> 00:03:55.291
<b>that the cause of mental confusion </b>
<b>isn't just external temptations; </b>

59
00:03:55.291 --> 00:04:02.041
<b>in reality, the cause is directionlessness, </b>
<b>the lack of a purpose.</b>

60
00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:05.125
<b>Understand it this way</b>

61
00:04:05.125 --> 00:04:08.000
<b>you leave home in your vehicle, </b>

62
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.000
<b>but</b>

63
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.666
<b>without any destination fixed.</b>

64
00:04:11.666 --> 00:04:12.666
<b>In such a case,</b>

65
00:04:12.666 --> 00:04:17.208
<b>sometimes one path will </b>
<b>tempt you, sometimes another.</b>

66
00:04:17.208 --> 00:04:19.791
<b>For a while this feels good,</b>

67
00:04:19.791 --> 00:04:25.166
<b>and in this pleasure, this temptation,</b>
<b>you keep wandering.</b>

68
00:04:25.166 --> 00:04:26.250
<b>But then</b>

69
00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:31.916
<b>while wandering, suddenly the fuel runs out,</b>

70
00:04:31.916 --> 00:04:33.500
<b>and now</b>

71
00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.083
<b>you realize</b>

72
00:04:35.083 --> 00:04:37.208
<b>the mistake.</b>

73
00:04:37.208 --> 00:04:40.291
<b>Now you can neither reach any destination,</b>

74
00:04:40.291 --> 00:04:43.416
<b>nor return home.</b>

75
00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:46.583
<b>This is just a simple example.</b>

76
00:04:46.583 --> 00:04:52.708
<b>But you can't live your </b>
<b>entire life this way, can you?</b>

77
00:04:52.708 --> 00:04:55.208
<b>So what's essential in life:</b>

78
00:04:55.208 --> 00:04:56.625
<b>First</b>

79
00:04:56.625 --> 00:04:58.416
<b>the right direction</b>

80
00:04:58.416 --> 00:05:01.166
<b>And what's needed for direction</b>

81
00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:06.250
<b> a clear and definite purpose </b>
<b>your destination</b>

82
00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:10.083
<b>If purpose and destination are clear,</b>

83
00:05:10.083 --> 00:05:11.750
<b>then direction will be clear,</b>

84
00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:14.000
<b>and if direction is clear,</b>

85
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.166
<b>then the mind won't become confused,</b>

86
00:05:16.166 --> 00:05:19.541
<b>its fuel won't run out,</b>

87
00:05:19.541 --> 00:05:23.125
<b>its strength won't be wasted.</b>

88
00:05:27.875 --> 00:05:29.416
<b>Today in the world,</b>

89
00:05:29.416 --> 00:05:35.500
<b>there are endless temptations pulling at </b>
<b>human attention and time. </b>

90
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:41.875
<b>Take this communication device in</b>
<b> your hand, for instance.</b>

91
00:05:41.875 --> 00:05:44.208
<b>How much time gets wasted.</b>

92
00:05:44.208 --> 00:05:48.625
<b>Focus seems to be almost disappearing.</b>

93
00:05:48.625 --> 00:05:52.166
<b>This is negatively affecting everyone, </b>

94
00:05:52.166 --> 00:05:55.916
<b>whether young or old.</b>

95
00:05:55.916 --> 00:05:58.583
<b>Everyone has numerous options.</b>

96
00:05:58.583 --> 00:06:04.875
<b>What to watch, what to listen to, </b>
<b>what to buy, what to read.</b>

97
00:06:04.875 --> 00:06:09.416
<b>Some people consider having </b>
<b>so many options good,</b>

98
00:06:09.416 --> 00:06:10.666
<b>but</b>

99
00:06:10.666 --> 00:06:15.416
<b>there's also a truth that the</b>
<b>more options there are,</b>

100
00:06:15.416 --> 00:06:18.625
<b>the more confused the mind becomes,</b>

101
00:06:18.625 --> 00:06:22.291
<b>the less patience it retains.</b>

102
00:06:22.291 --> 00:06:24.458
<b>Consider this</b>

103
00:06:24.458 --> 00:06:28.166
<b>you went to the market to buy something.</b>

104
00:06:28.166 --> 00:06:29.125
<b>But</b>

105
00:06:29.125 --> 00:06:36.125
<b>there you saw so many options that you</b>
<b>bought not one but many items.</b>

106
00:06:36.125 --> 00:06:40.875
<b>Now in this, both time and money were wasted.</b>

107
00:06:40.875 --> 00:06:42.041
<b>However,</b>

108
00:06:42.041 --> 00:06:46.708
<b>if your purpose had been absolutely clear</b>

109
00:06:46.708 --> 00:06:48.333
<b> what to buy,</b>

110
00:06:48.333 --> 00:06:50.000
<b>how much to spend,</b>

111
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.416
<b>where to buy from</b>

112
00:06:52.416 --> 00:06:55.375
<b>then despite numerous options,</b>

113
00:06:55.375 --> 00:07:01.666
<b>you would have gone with focus and </b>
<b>brought back only what was needed.</b>

114
00:07:01.666 --> 00:07:05.708
<b>Neither time nor money </b>
<b>would have been wasted.</b>

115
00:07:05.708 --> 00:07:08.041
<b>Similarly in life,</b>

116
00:07:08.041 --> 00:07:10.625
<b>if purpose isn't clear,</b>

117
00:07:10.625 --> 00:07:12.416
<b>time will be wasted,</b>

118
00:07:12.416 --> 00:07:15.041
<b> willpower will be wasted,</b>

119
00:07:15.041 --> 00:07:19.083
<b>and in the end, you'll remain confused as ever.</b>

120
00:07:19.083 --> 00:07:21.000
<b>It's extremely important</b>

121
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.625
<b>to find your purpose,</b>

122
00:07:23.625 --> 00:07:30.750
<b>and help family and children</b>
<b>find their purpose too.</b>

123
00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:34.583
<b>And this purpose makes life meaningful.</b>

124
00:07:34.583 --> 00:07:41.958
<b>This alone saves life from becoming confused</b>
<b>by numerous options and temptations.</b>

125
00:07:46.333 --> 00:07:47.875
<b>What would happen</b>

126
00:07:47.875 --> 00:07:53.083
<b>if an extremely intelligent person</b>
<b>is made to sit idle?</b>

127
00:07:53.083 --> 00:07:56.750
<b>If an athlete is deprived of sports?</b>

128
00:07:56.750 --> 00:08:02.958
<b>If a wrestler is kept from exercise?</b>

129
00:08:02.958 --> 00:08:09.625
<b>They will all not only become weak</b>
<b>but also become dejected.</b>

130
00:08:09.625 --> 00:08:16.041
<b>An intelligent person needs </b>
<b>new problems and puzzles to solve.</b>

131
00:08:16.041 --> 00:08:20.583
<b>An athlete needs to keep improving </b>
<b>their performance.</b>

132
00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:29.333
<b>A wrestler needs to do harder and harder </b>
<b>exercises, lift heavier and heavier weights.</b>

133
00:08:29.333 --> 00:08:33.416
<b>These keep both their mind and body healthy.</b>

134
00:08:33.416 --> 00:08:36.166
<b>New challenges.</b>

135
00:08:36.166 --> 00:08:37.500
<b>New challenges </b>

136
00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:44.791
<b>are extremely necessary to increase </b>
<b>one's capability, to keep them sharp.</b>

137
00:08:44.791 --> 00:08:48.708
<b>This is extremely important </b>
<b>in professional life too.</b>

138
00:08:48.708 --> 00:08:54.208
<b>Seek continuous new challenges</b>
<b>for yourself and your colleagues. </b>

139
00:08:54.208 --> 00:08:57.625
<b>This is essential for professional sharpness.</b>

140
00:08:57.625 --> 00:09:04.083
<b>When there are challenges, focus will increase, </b>
<b>enthusiasm will grow, capability will expand.</b>

141
00:09:04.083 --> 00:09:07.250
<b>And after conquering challenges,</b>

142
00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:09.708
<b>confidence will also rise.</b>

143
00:09:09.708 --> 00:09:16.250
<b>And in such a state, you will never</b>
<b>feel directionless or confused.</b>

